    "explanation": "Both parties actually agree on the decisive measurement, and the platform's own telemetry settles it. On the question the driver argued first: he DID arrive. His GPS trace (EV-GPS-00617) places him 6.91 m from the pickup pin, with 24 qualifying fixes inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius, so POL-NS-01 limbs (a) and (b) and the POL-NS-02 proximity test are satisfied, and I record that. But the no-show fee needs all four limbs of POL-NS-01, and limb (c) fails. The clause measures the hold from the first qualifying in-geofence fix at 07:15:50, not from the driver's 07:15:52 'arrived' tap. His longest continuous in-geofence run was 230 seconds, ending when he cancelled at 07:19:50 — 70 seconds short of the 300-second STANDARD minimum set by fee_schedule and repeated in POL-NS-06. Limb (d) also fails on its own terms: although RIDER_NO_SHOW is one of the three codes the clause recognises, the clause requires termination at or after the moment the required dwell elapsed, and 07:19:50 is 60 seconds before the 300 seconds would have elapsed at 07:20:50. Either failure defeats the charge; the reason code the driver honestly selected does not cure the missing time. Under POL-NS-06 the shortfall makes the cancellation fee not chargeable and refunds it in full, whether or not the rider was present — this is strict liability, not a finding of dishonesty against the driver. The POL-NS-06(i) accumulation route is unavailable in any event: the only traffic advisory, EV-ADVIS-00617-01, is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT), and the trace shows a single in-geofence interval (run_count 1, no excursion). Because POL-NS-01 is not satisfied in full, the 80 percent driver compensation under POL-NS-07 (which would have been SGD 3.20 of the SGD 4.00 line) is not payable; the anti-farming check is not reached and does not trip on these figures. The arrival marker itself was genuine — 6.91 m from the pin, trace peaking at 13.0 km/h against the 15 km/h motion threshold — so no false-arrival finding or POL-NS-05(ii) referral attaches to this trip. The rider's presence track (within 11.3 m of the pin across all 28 fixes, 07:15:40 to 07:19:43) corroborates her account but is not needed for the outcome, and POL-NS-04 is not available to her because EV-CHAT-00617 holds zero messages, so the last-four-digits exchange at the kerb is word against word and I draw nothing from it either way. Money: the fare breakdown (EV-FARE-00617) carries a single cancellation_fee line of SGD 4.00, total_charged SGD 4.00, payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00, against the STANDARD zone-class fee of SGD 4.00 and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee of SGD 4.00. A full refund returns that SGD 4.00 line to the rider and nothing further. No evidence artifact meets any of the POL-NS-08(a)-(d) impairment limbs, no POL-NS-09 escalation trigger fires, and the ruling rests on artifacts at weight 1.0.",
